{
  "$comment": "Three-layer perf gate (DECISIONS 2026-07-19, operator-approved). Layer 1: deterministic byte/count budgets — exact, zero-variance, the primary regression tripwires; values = measured 2026-07-19 baselines + headroom (see DECISIONS for the baseline table). Layer 2: statistical metrics asserted on the MEDIAN of 3 runs — thresholds unchanged; aggregationMethod is set explicitly because the LHCI default ('optimistic' = best-of-N) would silently weaken the gate. Layer 3 (escalation rule) lives in DECISIONS. Budgets only tighten without operator approval — loosening one is a flagged, operator-gated change. 2026-08-18 (operator-approved after the flag, DECISIONS same date): assertions became an assertMatrix so the /services + /styleguide photo-card menu (12 full-retina arch cards; LH's full-page scroll fetches every lazy card) gets a scoped image/total carve-out on exactly those two URLs; every other page keeps the original budgets, which stay the house defaults for any new page. Same day, rev 2: the compact-tile shrink let the carve-out TIGHTEN from 640/940KB to 384/512KB (measured 298/317KB — budgets only move down without a flag). 2026-09-03, BRANCH-SCOPED (feat/home-scale-rhythm, the home concept test; DECISIONS 2026-09-03 addendum): the operator lifted the zero-JS rule for this branch, and because the PR preview workflow runs these gates before it deploys, the lift has to reach the gate or there is no preview — so the HOME URL ALONE gets a third row identical to the house defaults except the script budget, raised from 30KB to 80KB for the self-hosted GSAP + Lenis layer (measured 66,188 B). Every other page keeps the house row. 2026-09-04: the concept was ADOPTED (operator: merge #179; DECISIONS 2026-09-03, the home entry's adoption paragraph) — this row is a STANDING carve-out for the home URL alone, the /services + /styleguide precedent: script 81,920 B for the self-hosted GSAP + Lenis motion layer (measured 69,155 B); every other page keeps the house row and its 30KB.",
